<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Villefranche-sur-Mer</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Villefranche-sur-Mer is a coastal town just east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a>, on one of the deepest natural harbours of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. Founded as a free town by Charles II of Anjou around 1295, it passed to Savoy with Nice in 1388 and became the dukes' main naval base, defended by the Citadel of Saint-Elme built in the 1550s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/villefranche-sur-mer.jpg" alt="Villefranche-sur-Mer" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Patrice Semeria · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Villefranche-s-Mer-VueSurLeVillage-20071102.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
